#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186678417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068918 :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Quotients Containing Trigonometric Functions Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9269a841-cb22-57b2-a1b9-ab5722aaacb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\left(\\ln\\left|\\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + 2\\right|\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9269a841-cb22-57b2-a1b9-ab5722aaacb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3\\left(\\ln\\left|\\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + 2\\right|\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678396} :answer-field/id #uuid "36cdbfc0-1dbe-5184-9526-131f920264cf" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186678364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bfed7b75-cd14-5de2-9aa5-2a0b83a01ce0" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + 2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int 1/u\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\ln\\left|u\\right|+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + 2$. Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}.\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{3 \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + 2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-3\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate with respect to $u$:\n\n$$\n-3\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=-3\\left(\\ln\\left|u\\right|\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n-3\\left(\\ln\\left|\\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + 2\\right|\\right)+C.\n$$"}]}
